{{/*
	Every optional block below is written as "{{ with ... -}}", its content,
	a blank line, then "{{ end -}}". The "-}}" on each action eats the
	newline ending its own line, so a block contributes exactly its content
	plus one blank line when it renders and exactly nothing when it does
	not: that is what keeps a skipped section from leaving its blank lines
	behind. The stamp above is followed directly by whatever comes first,
	and renderReadme trims the close back to a single newline.

	The badge row is not optional — a repository always has coverage worth
	showing its owner — so only the badges that need an audience are
	conditional, and each badge is written once.

	The footer is two blocks, not one: Additional Information renders for a
	private repository too, because the documents it links sit beside the
	README and anybody who can see one can open the other, while
	Contributing and License are addressed to an audience a private
	repository does not have.

	Inside "{{ with .OpenAPI }}" the dot is the parsed API description, so
	the "{{ .OpenAPI }}" reading off it there is that document's own openapi
	field: the version of the specification it conforms to, which is what a
	badge labelled OpenAPI is claiming. The API's own version lives at
	.Info.Version and would say something else entirely.
*/ -}}
